CFG231 A4 -- G2: linear growth and CMB
  repo = <repo>   (constants and controls import <repo>/campaign_fresh_gravity/CFG44_fluid_target/Bcommon.py read-only)
  mode = MAIN;  a0 footings: canonical 9.3603e-11, alt 1.1312e-10 m/s^2;  H0 = 67.4, Omega_L = 0.685
  a_V(H_Lambda) = 9.0328e-11, a_V(H0) = 1.0914e-10 m/s^2;  kappa = 1/2 FITTED; nothing here says the theory is closed or that data favour it.

======================================================================================================================
G2.1  the equations (declared reading) and the check of the frozen hand values y_lin = g_lin/a0 at k = 30 and 0.1 /Mpc, z = 0, delta = 1
======================================================================================================================
  drag reading: baryons source E through the Gauss law D(E) = g_N,b (Newtonian field of the BARYON perturbation g_b = f_b g_lin, f_b = Omega_b/Omega_m = 0.1564) and feel g_N + E;
  the cold component feels g_N only.  Quasi-static equations (sub-horizon): d''_c + 2H d'_c = 4 pi G rho_m (delta_m) ,  d''_b + 2H d'_b = 4 pi G rho_m delta_m + (div E)/(-1)...:
  the total-matter growth is changed by  Delta_tot = f_b psi(f_b g_lin)/g_lin  and the baryon force by  Delta_b = psi(g_b)/g_b  (both at fixed delta; the linear theory about E = 0 is strongly coupled, so delta is an INPUT).
  y_lin(z = 0, delta = 1, k = 30/Mpc) = 2.48e-05 (CFG172's hand value 2.5e-5);  y_lin(k = 0.1/Mpc) = 7.43e-03 (8e-3)
  [PASS] G2.1 the quasi-static input y_lin reproduces CFG172's hand values (2.5e-5 at k = 30, 8e-3 at k = 0.1) within 10%
         2.48e-05, 7.43e-03

