G2.4  no-cold reading: baryon-only sourcing in the same background (no emergent force), and the emergent force's own no-cold estimate
======================================================================================================================
  growth D(a = 1)/D(a = 1e-3): LCDM (Omega_m = 0.3153) 0.709;  baryon-only source (Omega_b = 0.0493) 0.012;  ratio baryons/LCDM = 0.017
  The no-cold reading needs the emergent sector to supply cold-like growth from a homogeneous background where E = 0 and the linear stiffness vanishes; no perturbation equation exists in class V about E = 0 (A3.6): UNDEFINED.
  y_lin(z = 1000, k = 30, delta = 1) = 2.48e+01 (>> 1: the Newtonian regime), so at the CMB epoch the K-law modification is small (Delta_tot = 2.9e-03 for K1 at k = 30); the estimate does NOT by itself exclude the CMB epoch, but no Boltzmann treatment exists, so the CMB part is UNDEFINED. (My first-draft narrative that the force would be 'enormous' at z ~ 1000 was wrong; corrected before this was recorded.)

